2. What you may do
   (a) View this repository on GitHub, and use and fork it only to the extent that the GitHub
       Terms of Service ("Section D.5 License Grant to Other Users") grant to GitHub users for
       public repositories, and only through GitHub's functionality.
   (b) Any use that is permitted by applicable copyright law without the Author's permission
       (for example, quotation within the limits of the law).

3. What you may not do without the Author's prior written permission
   Copy, reproduce, modify, adapt, translate, create derivative works of, distribute, publish,
   sublicense, sell, or otherwise use the contents of this repository, in whole or in part,
   outside the scope of Section 2. This includes, without limitation, use for commercial
   purposes, use in other products or services, and use as data for training machine
   learning models. Forks made under Section 2(a) do not grant any additional rights.

4. Third-party materials (not owned by the Author)
   (a) Drug names used in the synthetic data and in some evaluation records are derived from
       the "Drug Price Standard listed items" published by the Ministry of Health, Labour and
       Welfare of Japan (https://www.mhlw.go.jp/topics/2026/04/tp20260401-01.html), which is
       provided under the Public Data License (Version 1.0) (PDL1.0). The source data file
       itself is not included in this repository. Use of those portions is governed by PDL1.0,
       not by this notice. This repository is not created or endorsed by the Ministry.
   (b) Drug product names are trademarks or registered trademarks of their respective owners.
       Amazon Web Services, AWS, Amazon Bedrock, Claude, Anthropic, GitHub, and Tesseract are
       trademarks of their respective owners. Their use here is for identification only and
       does not imply endorsement.
   (c) Third-party software referenced by this repository (for example, packages listed in
       pyproject.toml and uv.lock) is governed by its own license and is not redistributed here.

5. Not a medical device; no clinical use
   This repository is an evaluation of OCR on synthetic (fictitious) prescriptions for personal
   learning. It is not a medical device and must not be used for diagnosis, treatment,
   dispensing, or any other clinical or pharmaceutical decision.

6. No warranty; limitation of liability
   THE CONTENTS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
